From dab9532c7a225ada60c798ce1658163b95e5be70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:24:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf: VU0 micro programs through the decoding interpreter

VCALLMS ran VU0 programs in the exact loop, which decodes each
instruction on every step and does soft-float arithmetic: about 9% of
the EE thread in a UN5 battle on the Switch. They now take the
interpreter VU1 falls back to (decoded once per code change, native
single precision with denormals flushed and overflow clamped).
PS2_VU0_EXACT=1 keeps the exact loop (PS2_VU_EXACT still covers both).

UN5 on the Mac: battle replay 8 s -> 6 s headless, its frames identical
to the exact loop's; the regression suite (battle, movie, shop, adv)
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/src/vu_micro.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/src/vu_micro.cpp b/runtime/src/vu_micro.cpp
index a109546..860f0ae 100644
--- a/runtime/src/vu_micro.cpp
+++ b/runtime/src/vu_micro.cpp
@@ -1309,7 +1309,11 @@ void run_fast(int n, std::uint32_t address) {
 
 void run(int n, std::uint32_t address) {
     static const bool exact = std::getenv("PS2_VU_EXACT") != nullptr;
-    if (n == 1 && !exact) {
+    // VU0 micro programs (VCALLMS) took the exact loop too, which decodes
+    // every instruction each time and does soft-float arithmetic: about 9% of
+    // the EE thread in a UN5 battle on the Switch. PS2_VU0_EXACT keeps it.
+    static const bool exact0 = exact || std::getenv("PS2_VU0_EXACT") != nullptr;
+    if (n == 1 ? !exact : !exact0) {
         interpret(n, address);
         return;
     }
